/-!
# Base change and the geometric fibre functor preserve finite coproducts

Let `X` be a scheme. The two remaining open assertions around the category `FÉt_X` of schemes
finite étale over `X` are both *right* exactness statements: that the base-change functor
`FÉt_Y ⥤ FÉt_X` of a morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` preserves finite colimits (the fourth assertion of
Stacks Tag 0BN9), and that the geometric fibre functor `F_x : FÉt_X ⥤ Type` preserves finite
colimits (the colimit half of the `exact` axiom of
`CategoryTheory.IsGaloisCategory`, hence the sixth and last field of Stacks Tag 0BNB).

This file proves the **coproduct half of both**, which is the half that needs no descent. A finite
coproduct in `FÉt_X` is the disjoint union of schemes
(`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isColimitSigmaCocone`), finite coproducts of schemes are *universal*
(`CategoryTheory.FinitaryPreExtensive Scheme`, which Mathlib proves), and base change is a
pullback, so the base change of the disjoint union is the disjoint union of the base changes. The
fibre functor inherits this because, through the factorisation
`F_x ≅ (base change along x) ⋙ coyoneda (𝟙_{Spec Ω})` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FundamentalGroup/EtaleFundamental/GaloisCategoryAxioms.lean`,
the corepresentable factor already preserves *all* finite colimits.

## What this leaves open, and why it is exactly one statement

By `CategoryTheory.Limits.preservesFiniteColimits_of_preservesCoequalizers_and_finiteCoproducts`,
finite colimits in `FÉt_X` are generated by its finite coproducts and its coequalizers, both of
which exist there. So after this file each of the two open assertions is reduced from
`PreservesFiniteColimits` to `PreservesColimitsOfShape WalkingParallelPair`, i.e. to *preservation
of coequalizers alone*; the two reductions are
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_preservesCoequalizers`
and
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor_of_preservesCoequalizers`,
stated here with that preservation as the single remaining hypothesis.

The coequalizer half is genuinely harder and is **not** proved here, nor anywhere in this
repository. A coequalizer in `FÉt_X` is the relative spectrum of the equalizer algebra
`𝓐 = Eq(a^♯, b^♯)` (`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isColimit_finiteEtaleCofork`), so the missing
statement is that forming that equalizer commutes with base change — equivalently that the
quotient of `𝓐 ⊂ 𝓒 = Z_* 𝒪` is a flat `𝒪_X`-module, which holds because `Z ⟶ Spec_X 𝓐` is
again finite étale and the trace form of a finite étale algebra splits the unit. Carrying that out
needs the base-change isomorphism for relative Spec, which
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeSpecBaseChange/BaseChange.lean` records as unproved.

## Main results

* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isPullback_finiteEtaleBaseChange_map_left` — the defining square of
  base change is cartesian in the cover: `A ×_Y X ⟶ B ×_Y X` is the base change of `A ⟶ B` along
  the projection `B ×_Y X ⟶ B`.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleBaseChange` — **base change of
  finite étale covers preserves finite coproducts**, the coproduct half of the fourth assertion of
  Stacks Tag 0BN9.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor` — **the geometric
  fibre functor preserves finite coproducts**, the coproduct half of the one open axiom of Stacks
  Tag 0BNB.
* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_preservesCoequalizers`
  and its fibre-functor analogue, in the same namespace,
  `preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor_of_preservesCoequalizers` — the two open
  assertions, reduced to preservation of coequalizers.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks]` attribute appears here: neither 0BN9 nor 0BNA nor 0BNB is completed by this file,
and the audit scanner keys on the bare four-character tag, so an attribute on a partial result
reports the whole tag formalized.

Universality of finite coproducts is taken from Mathlib's `FinitaryPreExtensive Scheme` instance
rather than from the repository's own `private` `IsUniversalColimit` lemmas for arbitrary index
types in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/Scheme/FamilyCoproduct.lean`, because the shapes
needed here are finite and the Mathlib statement is public.

The cartesian square is stated for an arbitrary morphism of schemes. The file
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FundamentalGroup/EtaleFundamental/GaloisCategoryAxioms.lean` contains a `private` copy of it specialised to a
geometric point (`baseChange_left_isPullback`); the general statement is what the coproduct
argument needs, since it is applied to the inclusions of a disjoint union.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BN9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BN9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BNA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BNA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BNB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BNB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.FundamentalGroup

/-- **The defining square of base change is cartesian in the cover.** For a morphism
`f : X ⟶ Y` of schemes and a morphism `φ : A ⟶ B` of finite étale covers of `Y`, the square
```
A ×_Y X ⟶ B ×_Y X
   |          |
   v          v
   A    ⟶    B
```
whose horizontal arrows are `φ` and its base change and whose vertical arrows are the first
projections, is a pullback square. -/
theorem isPullback_finiteEtaleBaseChange_map_left {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    {A B : FiniteEtaleOver Y} (φ : A ⟶ B) :
    IsPullback ((finiteEtaleBaseChange f).map φ).left
      (pullback.fst A.hom f) (pullback.fst B.hom f) φ.left := by
  have hsnd : ((finiteEtaleBaseChange f).map φ).left ≫ pullback.snd B.hom f
      = pullback.snd A.hom f := by
    simp only [finiteEtaleBaseChange, MorphismProperty.Over.pullback_map_left]
    exact pullback.lift_snd _ _ _
  have hfst : ((finiteEtaleBaseChange f).map φ).left ≫ pullback.fst B.hom f
      = pullback.fst A.hom f ≫ φ.left := finiteEtaleBaseChange_map_left_fst f φ
  have houter : IsPullback (((finiteEtaleBaseChange f).map φ).left ≫ pullback.snd B.hom f)
      (pullback.fst A.hom f) f (φ.left ≫ B.hom) := by
    rw [hsnd, MorphismProperty.Over.w φ]
    exact (IsPullback.of_hasPullback A.hom f).flip
  exact houter.of_right hfst (IsPullback.of_hasPullback B.hom f).flip

/-- **Stacks 0BN9, the coproduct half of the fourth assertion.** The base-change functor
`FÉt_Y ⥤ FÉt_X` of a morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` of schemes preserves finite coproducts.

A finite coproduct of finite étale covers is their disjoint union as schemes
(`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isColimitSigmaCocone`); finite coproducts of schemes are universal
colimits, so the cocone obtained from it by pulling back along `f` is again a colimit, and it is a
colimit in `FÉt_X` by `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isColimitOfIsColimitCoconeLeft`. The squares
required by universality are `isPullback_finiteEtaleBaseChange_map_left` at the inclusions of the
disjoint union. -/
instance preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleBaseChange {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    PreservesFiniteCoproducts (finiteEtaleBaseChange f) := by
  refine ⟨fun n => ⟨fun {D} => ?_⟩⟩
  refine preservesColimit_of_preserves_colimit_cocone (isColimitSigmaCocone Y D) ?_
  refine isColimitOfIsColimitCoconeLeft _ ?_
  refine ((FinitaryPreExtensive.isUniversal_finiteCoproducts
      (coproductIsCoproduct'
        (D ⋙ MorphismProperty.Over.forget finiteEtale ⊤ Y ⋙ Over.forget Y)))
    (coconeLeft ((finiteEtaleBaseChange f).mapCocone (sigmaCocone Y D)))
    (Discrete.natTrans fun j => pullback.fst (D.obj j).hom f)
    (pullback.fst (sigmaCocone Y D).pt.hom f) ?_ (NatTrans.Equifibered.of_discrete _)
    (fun j => isPullback_finiteEtaleBaseChange_map_left f ((sigmaCocone Y D).ι.app j))).some
  ext j
  exact (finiteEtaleBaseChange_map_left_fst f ((sigmaCocone Y D).ι.app j)).symm

/-- **Stacks 0BNB, the coproduct half of the one open Galois-category axiom.** The geometric fibre
functor of a scheme preserves finite coproducts.

Through the factorisation of the fibre functor as base change along the geometric point followed
by the functor corepresented by the identity cover of the point, the second factor preserves all
finite colimits (the covers of the spectrum of a separably closed field are the finite sets) and
the first preserves finite coproducts by
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleBaseChange`. -/
@[sga "1 XIII 2.1.3" "Clause of G5", sga "5 VI 1.2.3.1" "partial"]
theorem preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (x : GeometricPoint X) : PreservesFiniteCoproducts (finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x) := by
  have hco : PreservesFiniteColimits
      (coyoneda.obj (op (finiteEtalePointId x.residueField))) :=
    pointCoyoneda_preservesFiniteColimits x.residueField
  refine ⟨fun n => ?_⟩
  have hcomp : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete (Fin n))
      (finiteEtaleBaseChange x.hom ⋙
        coyoneda.obj (op (finiteEtalePointId x.residueField))) := inferInstance
  exact preservesColimitsOfShape_of_natIso (fiberIsoPointCoyoneda x).symm

/-- **The fourth assertion of Stacks 0BN9, reduced to coequalizers.** Since `FÉt_Y` has finite
coproducts and coequalizers and base change preserves the former, base change preserves finite
colimits as soon as it preserves coequalizers. -/
theorem preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleBaseChange_of_preservesCoequalizers
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    [PreservesColimitsOfShape WalkingParallelPair (finiteEtaleBaseChange f)] :
    PreservesFiniteColimits (finiteEtaleBaseChange f) :=
  preservesFiniteColimits_of_preservesCoequalizers_and_finiteCoproducts _

/-- **The one open axiom of Stacks 0BNB, reduced to coequalizers.** Since `FÉt_X` has finite
coproducts and coequalizers and the geometric fibre functor preserves the former, it preserves
finite colimits — the last of the six axioms of `CategoryTheory.IsGaloisCategory` for
`FÉt_X` — as soon as it preserves coequalizers. -/
theorem preservesFiniteColimits_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor_of_preservesCoequalizers
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (x : GeometricPoint X)
    [PreservesColimitsOfShape WalkingParallelPair (finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x)] :
    PreservesFiniteColimits (finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x) :=
  have := preservesFiniteCoproducts_finiteEtaleFiberFunctor x
  preservesFiniteColimits_of_preservesCoequalizers_and_finiteCoproducts _

end Stacks.FundamentalGroup

end
